<title>BELGIUM: EU vets C&amp;W/Bell Canada/Nynex cable TV deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets C&amp;W/Bell Canada/Nynex cable TV deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it was starting a preliminary probe into a proposal by Bell Canada International Inc, Cable and Wireless Plc and Nynex Corporation to share control in C&amp;W's cable television unit.</p>
<p>It said the deal was submitted for clearance on November 13 under the European Union's merger regulation 4064/89.</p>
<p>It has about a month from that date to clear the operation or start a four-month in-depth probe.</p>
<p>The Commission is also vetting another deal by which C&amp;W, the British telecommunications operator, and BCE Inc acquire joint control of Bell Cablemedia Plc and Videotron Holdings Plc. These last two companies are also active in telecoms and cable TV.</p>
</text>
